From c9c219d9adf18be42fce1029e7263235dcdd4621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:26:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Manage the browser add-on from the Updates tab

The Updates tab gains an Optional add-ons section for the browser
source: download and install, update, remove, undo, and restart to
apply. Changes are staged under addons-pending and applied by the
frontend on the next start, before any module loads; the frontend then
loads the add-on only when its manifest names this OBS base and
architecture and it is signed by the app's certificate, and otherwise
adds obs-browser to the disabled modules.

The Swift core finds the add-on in the running version's addons.json
(checked against the release digest), downloads it, checks its SHA-256,
manifest and signature, and stages it. When an app update moves to
another OBS base, the matching add-on is staged with it before the
update is ready; if that fails, the update still goes ahead and says so.

Tested by unit tests and two end-to-end tests (e2e-addon.mjs and
e2e-addon-update.mjs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
